  "raw": " could \"very easily trigger\" a by-election.\n\nZille took to Twitter on Wednesday morning - on the day Parliament was due to debate and pass the EE Bill - to accuse President Cyril Ramaphosa of putting “his foot in his mouth” before adding that no South African president would consider any kind of pay equity legislation as it will be “deadly” touching female genitalia or boobs.\n\nBut activists told News24 they shared Zille’s outrage at what they saw as a missed opportunity to introduce the requisite gender law reform closer to and parallelwith the recent March 8 violence.\n\nThe EE Bill touches on discrimination affecting women and the lesbian community in the workplace and business spheres, in terms of being paid less than their male counterparts for equal work.\n\nMany activists say an amendment should have addressed workers such as domestic workers and the gig economy, among others.\n\nNews24 reached out to Zille to ask her personally if",
